or her command;
(c) to monitor if DASSO members carry
out their duties in accordance with the
laws, orders and other instructions in
force and that they are characterised by
good conduct;
(d) to collaborate with other security
organs;
(e) to perform any other duty as may be
determined by the law;
(f) to perform any other activities assigned
by superior authorities, related to his or
her responsibilities;
(g) raising awareness on activities carried
out by DASSO;
(h) to submit regularly a report of DASSO
activities to his or her superiors.
